th, td { border: 1px solid #9aa5b4; padding: 4pt 8pt; text-align: left; }
</style></head>
<body><h1>Capelli Sport — CS Certification Exam · Set 4</h1>
<p><strong>Name: ____________________   Date: __________   Score: ______ / 100</strong></p>
<p>Closed book. Answer in the voice of the agent handling the ticket. For each scenario, state <strong>how you handle it</strong> (route + action) and <strong>the one trap</strong> that would fail the ticket. <strong>Section A — 6 points each; Section B (multiple choice) — 2 points each. Total 100.</strong></p>
<hr>
<p><strong>Q1.</strong> <em>"The other girls on my daughter's team already got their uniforms, but ours is held up. Can you tell me which pieces of our order are ready and which we're still waiting on?"</em> How do you handle a partial/held order?</p>
<p><strong>Q2.</strong> <em>"How long until my referee club order ships? It's been a week."</em> What timeline do you quote, and how do you confirm it?</p>
<p><strong>Q3.</strong> <em>"My son wore his new windbreaker once and the reflective dots on the shoulder are already damaged."</em> Is a non-decoration item covered? What do you do first, and what size do you replace with?</p>
<p><strong>Q4.</strong> <em>"The training top I ordered doesn't fit — it's too big. It's unworn with the tags on. How do I return it?"</em> State the return policy and address.</p>
<p><strong>Q5.</strong> <em>"It's been about 9 weeks, my order never arrived, and the season is basically over now. I just want a full refund."</em> How do you handle a never-received order when the need has passed?</p>
<p><strong>Q6.</strong> <em>"Can you just add a pair of socks to the order I placed yesterday? I forgot them."</em> What's the correct answer?</p>
<p><strong>Q7.</strong> <em>"I need my son's player link to place his order — can you send it to me?"</em>  (Assume his roster entry <strong>is</strong> in our system.) How do you handle this?</p>
<p><strong>Q8.</strong> <em>"The size Medium I want is out of stock with no restock date. What are my choices?"</em> Lay out the options you'd offer.</p>
<p><strong>Q9.</strong> <em>"Just give me the replacement order number you created so I can track it myself."</em> How do you respond?</p>
<p><strong>Q10.</strong> <em>"This is false advertising. My order is months past what you promised. If you won't get it here faster, the least you can do is refund my shipping."</em> How do you handle the shipping-refund request, and what has to happen before you promise it?</p>
<hr>
<h2>Section B — Multiple Choice (Q11–Q30)</h2>
<p>Choose the single best answer. 2 points each.</p>
<p><strong>11.</strong> Changing a player's number after ordering requires:</p>
<ul><li>A) An instant edit</li><li>B) Coach confirmation + putting the order on hold (only if not in production)</li><li>C) A refund</li><li>D) A new account</li></ul>
<p><strong>12.</strong> To put an order on hold for a number change, you email:</p>
<ul><li>A) ROLO</li><li>B) The club</li><li>C) Operations</li><li>D) Planning</li></ul>
<p><strong>13.</strong> A duplicate-order cancellation refund is handled via:</p>
<ul><li>A) The refunds team on BigCommerce</li><li>B) The club</li><li>C) PayPal</li><li>D) Shopify only</li></ul>
<p><strong>14.</strong> A customer is flexible and their item is OOS. Best:</p>
<ul><li>A) Offer an alternative size/color, or cancel+refund/wait</li><li>B) Auto-cancel</li><li>C) Ship anything available</li><li>D) Ignore it</li></ul>
<p><strong>15.</strong> A photo of the defect is required so we can:</p>
<ul><li>A) Bill the customer</li><li>B) Verify and process the correct replacement</li><li>C) Close faster</li><li>D) Refund shipping</li></ul>
<p><strong>16.</strong> "We do not offer expedited shipping" applies to:</p>
<ul><li>A) Only Shopify</li><li>B) Only team kits</li><li>C) All orders</li><li>D) International only</li></ul>
<p><strong>17.</strong> FBPA stands for:</p>
<ul><li>A) Fulfilled By USA</li><li>B) Fulfilled By Pennsylvania</li><li>C) Fast Priority Air</li><li>D) Fulfilled By Partner Agency</li></ul>
<p><strong>18.</strong> A backpack/equipment defect replacement may need:</p>
<ul><li>A) Internal (DM) approval before it's created</li><li>B) Nothing</li><li>C) A police report</li><li>D) The customer to pay</li></ul>
<p><strong>19.</strong> An order that never came and the season is over — you:</p>
<ul><li>A) Escalate for a refund/credit</li><li>B) Reship</li><li>C) Tell them to wait</li><li>D) Close it</li></ul>
<p><strong>20.</strong> On a return, the customer must include in the package:</p>
<ul><li>A) Only the item</li><li>B) Name, address, order #, reason</li><li>C) A photo</li><li>D) The RO number</li></ul>
<p><strong>21.</strong> A customer wants a manager's direct phone number. Correct:</p>
<ul><li>A) Provide it</li><li>B) Explain email-only support and escalate</li><li>C) Give a fake number</li><li>D) Refuse rudely</li></ul>
<p><strong>22.</strong> Restock requests are routed to:</p>
<ul><li>A) Planning (to replenish the SKU/size)</li><li>B) ROLO</li><li>C) The club</li><li>D) UPS</li></ul>
<p><strong>23.</strong> Which appears on the customer's statement for a refund?</p>
<ul><li>A) The club name</li><li>B) "CAPELLI SPORT"</li><li>C) "REFUND"</li><li>D) The bank's name</li></ul>
<p><strong>24.</strong> A partial/held order is often caused by:</p>
<ul><li>A) A defect</li><li>B) An added piece delaying the shipment</li><li>C) A wrong address</li><li>D) A cancellation</li></ul>
<p><strong>25.</strong> When is a hard delivery date promised to customers?</p>
<ul><li>A) Always</li><li>B) For tournaments</li><li>C) Never</li><li>D) On Shopify</li></ul>
<p><strong>26.</strong> Capelli shipped the wrong item — you resolve by:</p>
<ul><li>A) Evidence photo + ship the correct item</li><li>B) Return for refund</li><li>C) A direct exchange</li><li>D) No action</li></ul>
<p><strong>27.</strong> To ship an alternative on an OOS order, you should:</p>
<ul><li>A) Ship it automatically</li><li>B) Confirm with the customer first</li><li>C) Refund</li><li>D) Cancel</li></ul>
<p><strong>28.</strong> A club-wide billing error (a free item charged) is:</p>
<ul><li>A) Refunded instantly</li><li>B) Escalated to the internal team</li><li>C) Ignored</li><li>D) The customer's fault</li></ul>
<p><strong>29.</strong> Never share which with a customer?</p>
<ul><li>A) The tracking link</li><li>B) The club password</li><li>C) The return address</li><li>D) The processing time</li></ul>
<p><strong>30.</strong> The correct opener for a defective-decoration item acknowledges:</p>
<ul><li>A) A discount</li><li>B) Our strict quality checks and that it slipped past them</li><li>C) The RO number</li><li>D) The club</li></ul></body></html>